# FunBench seed tasks.
#
# A task has a prompt, a level, and one or more tests. The runner concatenates
# a candidate solution with each test, executes it, and compares stdout byte
# for byte with `expect`. Reference solutions live in solutions/<id>.fun and
# must pass with `run.fun --all`.

tasks
  -
    id hello
    level 0
    prompt Write `fun greet(name)` that returns `Hello, <name>!`.
    tests
      -
        code `?. greet('Ada');
`
        expect `Hello, Ada!
`
      -
        code `?. greet('Fun');
`
        expect `Hello, Fun!
`
  -
    id sum
    level 0
    prompt Write `fun sum(xs)` that returns the total of a numeric list; an empty list returns 0.
    tests
      -
        code `?. sum([1, 2, 3]);
`
        expect `6
`
      -
        code `?. sum([]);
`
        expect `0
`
  -
    id json-names
    level 0
    prompt Write `fun names(text)` that parses JSON with a `users` array and returns the list of `name` values in order.
    tests
      -
        code `var r = names('{"users":[{"name":"Ada"},{"name":"Bob"}]}');
?. r.@toJson();
`
        expect `["Ada","Bob"]
`
      -
        code `var r = names('{"users":[]}');
?. r.@toJson();
`
        expect `[]
`
  -
    id word-count
    level 1
    prompt Write `fun countWords(text)` that returns a map from each whitespace-separated word to its count.
    tests
      -
        code `var m = countWords('a b a');
?. m.a;
?. m.b;
`
        expect `2
1
`
      -
        code `var m = countWords('one');
?. m.@has('one');
?. m.@has('two');
`
        expect `True
False
`
  -
    id class-point
    level 1
    prompt Define a class `Point(x, y)` with a method `sum()` returning `x + y`.
    tests
      -
        code `var p = Point(2, 3);
?. p.sum();
`
        expect `5
`
      -
        code `var p = Point(-1, 1);
?. p.sum();
`
        expect `0
`
